{"answerable":"yes","steps":[{"id":"ask-86513713-1","say":"For tenancies of two years or more, either side can bring the tenancy to an end early under break clauses. The tenant can end it with 3 months’ notice in writing.","actions":[{"type":"focus","target":"p41.s4"},{"type":"highlight","targets":["p41.s4"],"color":"yellow","at_word":10},{"type":"focus","target":"p42.s2","at_word":26},{"type":"highlight","targets":["p42.s2"],"color":"yellow","at_word":26}]},{"id":"ask-86513713-2","say":"Tenant cannot give notice in the first 3 months, so the earliest end is after 6 months. The landlord has a one-off break at 6 months, plus receiver and sale breaks needing at least 2 months notice. A sale needs at least 4 months from first warning, with evidence it is marketed. Overpaid rent is repaid within 14 days of the end if the tenant vacated.","actions":[{"type":"focus","target":"p42.s1"},{"type":"board","item":{"kind":"timeline","title":"Early ending notice periods","unit":"month","source":"document","events":[{"label":"Tenancy starts","at":0,"position":0},{"label":"Tenant may give notice","after":"Tenancy starts","offset":3,"offset_unit":"month","position":91.3125},{"label":"Earliest tenant end","after":"Tenancy starts","offset":6,"offset_unit":"month","position":182.625},{"label":"Landlord 6-month break","after":"Tenancy starts","offset":6,"offset_unit":"month","position":182.625},{"label":"Sale: 4 months warning","after":"Tenancy starts","offset":4,"offset_unit":"month","position":121.75}],"spans":[{"label":"3 months notice","from":"Tenant may give notice","length":3,"length_unit":"month","role":"notice","start":91.3125,"end":182.625}]}},{"type":"board_focus","part":1},{"type":"board_focus","part":3,"at_word":20},{"type":"board_focus","part":4,"at_word":38},{"type":"highlight","targets":["p42.s1"],"color":"yellow"},{"type":"focus","target":"p59.s11"},{"type":"highlight","targets":["p59.s11"],"color":"yellow"}]}],"followups":["When do break clauses apply?","How is overpaid rent repaid?"]}